<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Ui Fidgenti</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 1200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kingdom of west County Limerick whose king Donnubán sided with the Vikings of Limerick against Brian Bóruma, and from whom the O'Donovans descend.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Uí Fidgenti claimed descent from Fiachu Fidgenid, a kinsman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganachta</a>, and held much of what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-limerick">County Limerick</a> west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-maigue">Maigue</a> from the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a>. They formed a subject but partly privileged kingdom within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Kingdom of Munster</a>, divided into branches such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-chonaill-gabra">Uí Chonaill Gabra</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and the fertile lands south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-shannon">Shannon</a>. In the 10th century it was caught between the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-cais">Dál Cais of Thomond</a> and the Norse town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a>. Its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donnuban-mac-cathail">Donnubán mac Cathail</a> allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivar-of-limerick">Ivar of Limerick</a> and helped bring about the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mathgamain-mac-cennetig">Mathgamain</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Bóruma</a>, in 976, which drew Brian's revenge.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After Brian's victories the Uí Fidgenti were reduced, and in the late 12th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Norman</a> advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a>, especially by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fitzgerald-dynasty">FitzGeralds</a>, displaced them. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donnuban-mac-cathail">Donnubán</a>'s descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odonovan-family">O'Donovans</a>, moved south into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-cork">Cork</a>, where they held lordships near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skibbereen">Skibbereen</a> for centuries.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 450 CE – 1200 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:68.66%;width:14.93%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 1200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Donnubán mac Cathail</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish, later Middle Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Uí Fidgenti</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=825&amp;focus=ui-fidgenti" aria-label="Ui Fidgenti on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4505 374 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ui Fidgenti lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4823 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4825 630h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4825 630h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ireland. <a href="/atlas?year=825&amp;focus=ui-fid